---
// The About page's skyline (27 Nov 2026, the owner: "like the illustration in the pitch deck of Berlin's skyline, but
// all the cities we operate in"; then "a tiny bit more designed, so you know what the buildings are"): one line
// drawing on one baseline, in the deck's manner (flat shapes, fine outlines, a pale solid fill, a few lighter details),
// from left to right:
// Zürich: old town houses, the Grossmünster (twin towers, octagonal belfries, domed caps, clocks), the Fraumünster's
//   spire, St. Peter (the great clock);
// Berlin: the Brandenburg Gate (columns, quadriga), the TV tower (sphere with its window band, antenna), the Reichstag
//   (corner towers, portico, glass dome);
// Singapore: the Esplanade's two domes, two Supertrees, Marina Bay Sands (three towers, the SkyPark), the ArtScience
//   lotus;
// Dubai: the Burj Al Arab (sail, helipad), the Dubai Frame, the Burj Khalifa (setbacks, spire), the Emirates Towers.
// Decorative. In the indigo accent; it draws itself once on load, city by city (--c), and simply shows under reduced
// motion. It has no ground line of its own: the box ends exactly at the buildings' feet (y 392), so the page stands it
// on a rule (the About hero's credentials line).
const gateCols = [264, 286, 308, 330, 352, 374];
// three Marina Bay Sands towers, each a little narrower at the top; floor lines across them
const mbs = [658, 694, 730];
